A||||7||88 Database Nut||Hey '88 Owners and Fans, Please Read!||||7||
Z||000000||88 Database Nut||04-25-2000||01:29 PM||||Fellow Fiero Fans,<P>Just a short note to those who haven't heard of this project or wanted to contribute but may have forgotten about it.  We now have 1048 cars in the 1988 Fiero Database, only 8 from reaching the milestone of 4% of the cars produced in 1988.  What is the 1988 F.D.?<BR>This is a project I started last year in the hopes of eventually forming a registry of the '88s, so that when they become a collectible car in 2033 we will be ready. 8)  Unlike other worthy efforts, this is not intended to be an owners database, but a car database.  I need the VIN and a brief description (please include the factory colors and tranny type), and the status of the car (dead or alive).  Any other info is welcome too, but is not required.  Also, if you desire privacy, all references to you will be omitted (have done this several times already).<BR>So, if you own an 88 or used to, have a friend or relative with one, have seen one in a junkyard or 4sale, or have taken one apart, please take a minute to get the Info and send it to me.  It's just as important to know which cars are no longer around as it is to know which ones are still moving.<BR>For a fairly detailed listing of the 1048 cars in the database, please email me and I'll send you a copy.  You can see a slightly older copy at <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/motorcity/track/3487/index.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/motorcity/track/3487/index.html</A>   This is a friends' website which is full of good info, especially on '88s (Thanks Fiero5sp!).<P>My best to all Fiero Owners,<P>John Willhoff aka 88 Database Nut||||reg||7
